course: dictionary
lesson: 9171
title: Snub: ignored on purpose
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words carry a feeling inside them. To snub someone is to ignore them or treat them coldly on purpose, so they know you do not want to be friends. «Ruby felt snubbed when her friends walked past without saying hello.» The word snubbed tells you Ruby was hurt on purpose, not just forgotten.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. The words "without saying hello" show that the snub was deliberate. Ask yourself: did someone do this to hurt, or was it an accident? If it was done on purpose, snub is the word you need.
explain: A snub can also be a noun, something someone does: «It was a deliberate snub.» Here the snub is the act itself. In the news, leaders or teams can snub each other by refusing to meet or shake hands.
explain: Snub can also describe a nose. A snub nose is short and turned up at the end, so it has nothing to do with feelings. The same word can have different meanings, so check the sentence to see which one fits.
fact: To snub someone means to ignore them or treat them coldly on purpose.
fact: A snub is an act of ignoring or insulting someone in this way.
fact: A snub nose is short and turned up at the end.
fact: «Felt snubbed» means someone felt left out or insulted on purpose.
fact: Golden snub-nosed monkeys live in cold mountain forests in central China, often above 2,000 metres, and in winter they eat lichen, bark and buds.
exercise: «Her friends snubbed her at lunch.» What does snubbed mean? | Given a big hug | *Ignored on purpose | Served extra pudding | Sent home early
exercise: «It was a deliberate snub.» What is a snub in this sentence? | A type of cold drink | A game played in the playground | *An act of ignoring someone on purpose | A kind present
exercise: Golden snub-nosed monkeys have a nose that is short and turned up. What does snub nose mean? | Covered with bright feathers | *Short and turned up at the end | Long and thin like a stick | Very loud when it sneezes
test: What does it mean to snub someone? | To treat someone with warmth | To run after someone to say sorry | To sing a song for someone | *To ignore someone on purpose
test: «The leaders refused to shake hands, a clear snub.» What does snub mean here? | A winning goal | A friendly wave | *An insult shown by refusing to meet or greet | A long speech
exam: Which clue in «Ruby felt snubbed when her friends walked past without saying hello» shows the snub was on purpose? | Ruby felt | Her friends | *Walked past without saying hello | Ruby
